{
 "_what": "The Variable Index definitions: every adjustable variable the teardown records, where it is read from, its type, and how production can change it. Observed values are NOT here — they are computed per brand into runs/ad-variations/<brand>/variable-index/. A value the coder cannot place on a vocab list is kept as 'other: <label>' and shows in the index as a new value, never dropped.",
 "status": "draft",
 "curator": "the owner",
 "families": {
  "hook": "Hook — the first seconds",
  "structure": "Structure — framework, order, awareness",
  "audience": "Audience — who it speaks to (the audience read)",
  "proof": "Proof — how it shows it works",
  "product": "Product — what is shown, when",
  "talent": "Talent — who is on screen and how they sound",
  "look": "Look — places, wardrobe, camera",
  "sound": "Sound — voice, music, delivery",
  "edit": "Edit rhythm — length, shots, cuts",
  "text": "Text — captions and on-screen words",
  "ask": "Offer and ask — the close"
 },
 "cost_classes": {
  "free": "$0 — local on the Mac or a text layer",
  "$": "under $__ per variation",
  "$$": "$__ per variation",
  "$$$": "over $__ per variation",
  "reshoot": "needs a person to film it again"
 },
 "lock_lever_rule": "Computed per brand, not decided here. Among the brand's top-quartile posts by views: if one value holds 60% or more of their views, the variable is LOCK-LEANING (the winners converge on it); otherwise LEVER (the winners vary, so it can move). Text variables are always LEVER (wording). Numeric variables are read on their bins.",
